SECTION 4: DOCUMENT UPLOAD AND STATUS CONSISTENCY
==================================================

Review the existing document upload, repository, verification, approval, and submission workflows before introducing the new vault.

Preserve existing screens and workflows wherever possible.

## 4.1 Distinguish file contents from file metadata

A filename, MIME type, and file size do not constitute the actual document.

Inspect whether the existing application creates document records without retaining the actual selected File object.

Correct this inconsistency.

The frontend should distinguish between:
- The original document file.
- Document metadata.
- OCR-extracted text.
- Verification status.
- Approval status.
- Submission records associated with individual requests.

Do not claim that a document's contents have been stored when only its metadata has been saved.

## 4.2 Separate verification from approval

Keep these concepts distinct:

- Uploaded: The user submitted a file through the demo.
- Verification pending: The verification workflow has not been completed.
- Verified: The defined verification step has actually completed.
- Approval pending: The document is awaiting the appropriate reviewer decision.
- Approved: The appropriate approval action has been completed.
- Rejected: A reviewer has explicitly rejected the document.

Preserve existing status names and visual components wherever possible.

Do not automatically mark a document as approved when a timer finishes.

Do not treat OCR success as document verification.

Do not treat a successful file upload as approval.

Do not imply that a real-world authority or institution verified a document when no such service exists.

If verification is simulated, represent it honestly as a demo operation.

Ensure that status changes are consistent across the student profile, document repository, and institution-facing review screens.

